{"data": [{"author_id": "2260892328", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-11T00:12:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120308615382991292"], "id": "2120308615382991292", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Opus 5.5 was a huge jump for me, now Fable 5.2..", "url": "https://x.com/marketing_bloke/status/2120308615382991292"}, {"author_id": "881216417730895877", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:17:47.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120279783682781194"], "id": "2120279783682781194", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 10, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Not steep enough, should go hyperbolic eventually.", "url": "https://x.com/AlienVakeel/status/2120279783682781194"}, {"author_id": "1767136706459774976", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T21:17:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120264639577743717"], "id": "2120264639577743717", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Looks like robotics really goes in the LLM hole.", "url": "https://x.com/Grauwacht/status/2120264639577743717"}, {"author_id": "1904300658460688384", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:16:09.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120249172372684964"], "id": "2120249172372684964", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick 🌍\n\nTRAUNES AI is fighting misinformation through AI-powered fact-checking.\n\n🗳️ Support us in the Meta AI Hackathon Community Vote:\n\nhttps://t.co/DIb5tkfS8W\n\nEvery vote counts! 🙏", "url": "https://x.com/Lumiere65/status/2120249172372684964"}, {"author_id": "1486453404905922564", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:03:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120230780001554502"], "id": "2120230780001554502", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Remote Labor, which tests end-to-end freelance tasks, is the benchmark I care about most. Can it finish a real job? Which kinds of work are closest to being done well by AI today?", "url": "https://x.com/KionigMax/status/2120230780001554502"}, {"author_id": "1293233899640741888", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:53:02.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120228253457891483"], "id": "2120228253457891483", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 196, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick The timelines are funny (scary).  +8.8 points above trend.  2.5 weeks early!  What?!", "url": "https://x.com/munion_ryan/status/2120228253457891483"}, {"author_id": "1665069091", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:27:52.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120221922076274952"], "id": "2120221922076274952", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@terrydavies59 @emollick Agreed, Terry. For a small business the test is simple: did the job get done, and did I have to redo it? Curious which piece of administration it took off your plate first at the agency?", "url": "https://x.com/GWancheck/status/2120221922076274952"}, {"author_id": "2119417167049265152", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:22:35.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120220593467412631"], "id": "2120220593467412631", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 0, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick If it can already do full freelance jobs end to end, that makes landing a first gig even harder for beginner freelancers.", "url": "https://x.com/Allenco_SI/status/2120220593467412631"}, {"author_id": "82457051", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T18:12:16.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120217995847008543"], "id": "2120217995847008543", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 11, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@mark_myerson @emollick You know, one time I paid someone on Upwork $600 to transform a Zapier flow into a Google cloud function. So I see your point", "url": "https://x.com/connorshepherd/status/2120217995847008543"}, {"author_id": "2115841222103511040", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:32:24.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120207961498976593"], "id": "2120207961498976593", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 3, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Benchmarks that measure end to end freelance jobs and robotics control are the ones that matter now. A model that can do the whole job is a different thing from a model that can answer a question about the job.", "url": "https://x.com/ParthRaam/status/2120207961498976593"}, {"author_id": "2382909302", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:24:41.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120206022040277269"], "id": "2120206022040277269", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 5, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Clearly we're trending towards a total disruption of the white-collar labor market by ~2028...", "url": "https://x.com/JaitanMartini/status/2120206022040277269"}, {"author_id": "1365701888604184579", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:21:22.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120205184051601695"], "id": "2120205184051601695", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick The part that matters is Remote Labor, not the composite. If it can actually close freelance loops end-to-end, the benchmark stops being a party trick. How close was that \"end-to-end\" to something you'd actually pay for?", "url": "https://x.com/zuoshi_ai/status/2120205184051601695"}, {"author_id": "105447965", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:09:28.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120202191046897811"], "id": "2120202191046897811", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 20, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@eythorarnalds @emollick liftoff confirmed, we're just arguing about the exact launch date now", "url": "https://x.com/alsamahi/status/2120202191046897811"}, {"author_id": "1610317817558990848", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T17:06:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120201506137756159"], "id": "2120201506137756159", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 1, "like_count": 0, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 0}, "text": "@emollick Remote Labor is the one I watch from a staffing desk. Even as agents finish more freelance work end to end, someone still has to scope the job, judge the result, and own the client. That's a skill worth building now.", "url": "https://x.com/Don_Flowhire/status/2120201506137756159"}, {"author_id": "1461278862696861702", "conversation_id": "2120000888974766501", "created_at": "2026-11-10T16:44:21.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120195870515929403"], "id": "2120195870515929403", "public_metrics": {"bo